[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6551319986","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/875#issuecomment-6551319986","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/875","id":6551319986,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABhn01sg","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-01T00:43:26Z","updated_at":"2026-11-01T00:43:26Z","body":"The focused identity audit found an exact ontology term, so §3 step 1 takes precedence over the CAS fallback proposed in this issue: **NCIT:C61946 — Sodium Phosphate, Dibasic, Heptahydrate**. The inspected NCI EVS record is active in NCIt 26.10d and explicitly gives CAS 7782-85-6, formula `2Na.HO4P.7H2O`, and FDA UNII `70WT22SF4B`. [NCI EVS record](https://api-evsrest.nci.nih.gov/api/v1/concept/ncit/C61946?include=full); [FDA UNII record](https://precision.fda.gov/uniisearch/srs/unii/70WT22SF4B).\n\nPubChem resolves the CAS to CID 6096963 and supplies the complete seven-water formula `H15Na2O11P`, mass 268.07, and hydrate-specific structure. The current YAML InChI/SMILES instead match the anhydrous CHEBI:34683 bytes. Whole-form identity and the anhydrous parent must remain distinct; a retained parent/component annotation needs its own supported non-identity representation. The structure correction remains a separate scope from the primary-identity decision. [PubChem CAS resolution](https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/7782-85-6/cids/JSON); [PubChem properties](https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/cid/6096963/property/MolecularFormula,MolecularWeight,InChI,InChIKey,CanonicalSMILES/JSON); [ChEBI parent](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:34683).\n\nNo exact ChEBI heptahydrate was found in the bounded live searches by CAS, exact names, and all returned heptahydrate/hydrogenphosphate/sodium-phosphate results; this is not a universal absence claim. CAS Common Chemistry was unavailable (page 403, API 401), so its contents were not used. NCI, FDA and PubChem independently support the CAS association. An ignored-file-inclusive scan of maintained ingredient YAML found no second current owner of NCIT:C61946 or CAS 7782-85-6. The 0.02 M stock is a distinct concentration-qualified preparation and must remain separate.\n\n**Recommended implementation, after coordination:** promote the primary identifier and exact ontology grounding to NCIT:C61946 through the guarded writer and SSSOM receipt chain; retain the exact-form CAS as chemistry metadata; atomically move this record's existing rejection-ledger `mim_id` to NCIT:C61946 and correct its obsolete no-exact-term/CAS-only rationale. Keep CHEBI:34683 rejected as a unified identity. A new identifier alone grants no release approval.\n\n**Current blocker is the explicitly protected unified rebuild in PR #914.** At inspected head `8dc2f266ebf72959a5d2f601d1c767c9138db44f`, #914 does not change this target YAML or its aggregate record hunk. The heptahydrate rejection-ledger row is unchanged diff context, so merely sharing that ledger path is not a conflict. However, #914 directly changes the `Na2HPO4 x 7 H2O` unified row from 19 to 28 occurrences while retaining the local identifier. This promotion would change that same row and hydrate aliases, requiring a coordinated unified rebuild and provenance update. Applying the primary without its ledger update would also fail Claw's identity-consistency guard. No record or generated mapping was changed in this audit.\n\nThe options are therefore (1) retain the evidence and defer application while #914 owns that rebuild, or (2) agree a coordinated atomic identity/ledger/receipt/unified update. Option 1 preserves the current non-overlap instruction. Prior #863, #334 and #459 decisions were inspected; this recommendation does not silently undo their hydrate boundaries. The broader finding `SEM:cb9ec35166086d936f70` also covers structure and provisional BUFFER evidence, which this identity decision cannot retire.\n\nEvidence receipt: `output/sssom-curation-20261101T003435Z/audit875/` contains `audit875.json`, `audit875.md`, exact input hashes, primary-source response snapshots, bounded search results, prior issue comments, and the precise #914 diff. The audit is input to this batch's combined native review; it is not an independent release approval or a claim that all scientific review is complete. No paid research or provider credits were used.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6551319986/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6551512696","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/875#issuecomment-6551512696","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/875","id":6551512696,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABhoAmeA","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-01T01:02:40Z","updated_at":"2026-11-01T01:02:40Z","body":"The exact-NCIT finding and native scientific review are published as evidence in [PR #1007](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pull/1007). The recommendation remains NCIT:C61946 under section3 step1, supported by NCI/CAS/formula/UNII correspondence and PubChem hydrate structure. The record remains unchanged pending coordination with PR #914 on the same unified row and atomic identity/ledger/SSSOM update. Its inherited anhydrous structure and provisional BUFFER concerns are not closed. [Review and primary-source archive](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/blob/bf7d514c804670ea3db3e9e75a2c94624554fa26/reports/sssom_scientific_curation_20261101/README.md).\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6551512696/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6553802172","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/875#issuecomment-6553802172","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/875","id":6553802172,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABhqMVvA","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-01T05:14:24Z","updated_at":"2026-11-01T05:14:24Z","body":"The approved plan selects **NCIT:C61946 — Sodium Phosphate, Dibasic, Heptahydrate**, following MAPPING_SEMANTICS section 3 step 1. This supersedes the original proposed CAS fallback: an exact ontology term is available.\n\nThe official [NCI EVS response](https://api-evsrest.nci.nih.gov/api/v1/concept/ncit/C61946?include=full), inspected on 2026-11-01 at 04:19:28 UTC, remains active in NCIt 26.10d and gives CAS `7782-85-6`, formula `2Na.HO4P.7H2O`, and UNII `70WT22SF4B`. Its archived response SHA-256 is `a112c3e91dd6aa46feb112621ba5d13673df69f1b20665e042e22b8aa05a1d83`; the local NCIT canonical label agrees.\n\nThe bounded implementation will change this record's identifier and exact ontology grounding, migrate its existing rejection-ledger `mim_id` in the same commit, keep CHEBI:34683 rejected as a unified identity, replace the obsolete ontology/registry pair with one NCIT exactMatch through the guarded generation/receipt path, and rebuild the unified snapshot. Prior history, accepted hydrate aliases, source lineage, and unrelated claims will be preserved.\n\nThe mapping-change receipt adds no scientific approval. The inherited anhydrous InChI/SMILES and provisional BUFFER concerns remain open; this identity correction does not retire the broader semantic finding or merge the distinct concentration-qualified stock. Independent final-head review, full QC, receipt replay, and green queue checks are required before merge.\n\nApproved plan SHA-256: `99b7746742f70c7896ed163a833a8b214282dba84567dc3213ec0a2b194e4d90`.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6553802172/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6554058702","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/875#issuecomment-6554058702","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/875","id":6554058702,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABhqb_zg","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-01T05:45:09Z","updated_at":"2026-11-01T05:45:09Z","body":"Implemented in PR #1030 at `cb9f59a0d045f104ee2c3c00c8d6c4ad4f4eaf1f` under approved-plan step 2.\n\nThe exact NCIT:C61946 identity and rejection-ledger owner move together. The native receipt records one changed mapping and one removed registry row; the unified rebuild changes only the three heptahydrate spellings. #1028 permits verified position/evidence-key relocation for an otherwise unchanged companion cohort. #1029 now refuses false completion after reserved receipt or backup replacement and retains recovery evidence; independent native transaction probes and re-review pass.\n\n`just qc`, receipt replay, native invariants, the companion and supported-release gates, and focused tests pass. Independent final-head review is recorded at https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/pull/1030#issuecomment-6554056208 . Required remote checks are running; no merge has occurred.\n\nThis applies the approved exact-identity decision only. The new mapping remains WITHHOLD pending mapping-specific review, and inherited chemistry/BUFFER concerns remain OPEN. The broader #875 issue is deliberately not auto-closed by this PR.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6554058702/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6555609003","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/875#issuecomment-6555609003","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/875","id":6555609003,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABhr6nqw","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-01T09:36:17Z","updated_at":"2026-11-01T09:36:17Z","body":"Verified merge: PR #1030 landed as `b7313f9e4567ad1cedc8287d482cb04864a2f875` through the squash merge queue. All 16 PR checks and 16 merge-group checks passed; both full-suite runs reported 3427 passed and 83 skipped, with the maintained-package coverage gate at 71%. Independent verification confirmed all 469 reviewed PR paths in the landed tree and preservation of unrelated parent content. The owned feature branch was deleted after that verification.\n\nThe exact NCIT:C61946 identity, paired rejection-ledger owner, receipt, unified rebuild and 32 existing membership references are now on main. The live-cohort regression follows retired-identity absence rather than freezing the historical 32-row count (#1034); the original 32-row application remains reproduced from immutable evidence.\n\nThis issue remains open for inherited anhydrous structure and provisional BUFFER evidence. The new mapping remains WITHHOLD; neither the merge nor passing checks grants scientific release approval. Committed evidence: [identity review](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/tree/b7313f9e4567ad1cedc8287d482cb04864a2f875/reports/ncit_heptahydrate_875_20261101), [membership repair](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/tree/b7313f9e4567ad1cedc8287d482cb04864a2f875/reports/ncit_heptahydrate_875_20261101_membership), and [cohort-test follow-up](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/tree/b7313f9e4567ad1cedc8287d482cb04864a2f875/reports/ncit_heptahydrate_875_20261101_cohort_tests).\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6555609003/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]